# Rust
target/

# Node / frontend
node_modules/
dist/

# The development wiki. RHIZOLOG_ROOT defaults to ./wiki, so running the
# backend creates this — scratch content plus a derived SQLite index under
# .rhizolog/. None of it belongs in the repo.
backend/wiki/

# Rhizolog's derived index inside any wiki directory, including example-wiki/.
# It is built from the markdown beside it and rebuilds on startup.
#
# The database by name, not the whole directory: `.rhizolog/times/` sits beside
# it and is a time log, which is authored data with no other copy. A wiki kept
# in git should ignore these two lines and nothing more.
#
# `**/` because a pattern with a slash in it is anchored to this file's own
# directory: plain `.rhizolog/index.db` would miss `example-wiki/`'s.
**/.rhizolog/index.db
**/.rhizolog/index.db-*

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
*.log
